    "As seen in equation 4.24 our update in momentum is given by\n",
    "$$\n",
    "v_{k+1}=\\eta \\sum_{j=0}^k \\gamma^{k-j}\\nabla C(\\boldsymbol{\\theta}_j)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "If we have a flat direction with $\\eta\\lambda<<1$ each successive gradient point the same way and gets added by the equation above. We eventually get equation 4.25:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "v_{\\inf}=\\eta g \\sum_{j=0}^{\\inf} \\gamma^j=\\frac{\\eta g}{1-\\gamma}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "The steps are therefore increased by a factor of $(1-\\gamma)^{-1}$ which is between 0 and 1.\n",
    "FOr steep terms, gradient descent often oscilates between + and - to get to the bottom, but with momentum we that in 4.24 the steps of + and - will cancel each other out and oscillate less, thus slowing down."
   ]
